<title>USA: UPS, Teamsters begin new talks guided by mediator.</title>
<headline>UPS, Teamsters begin new talks guided by mediator.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>United Parcel Service and the Teamsters union began new talks on Thursday guided by a federal government mediator as a strike against the huge package delivery company entered its 11th day.</p>
<p>Teamsters union President Ron Carey and UPS chief negotiator Dave Murray arrived at a Washington hotel for the talks just after 9 a.m. EDT (1300 GMT). Labor Secretary Alexis Herman was expected to speak to the two sides at the opening of the talks.</p>
</text>
